quiet.md #25: survive GPU device loss on Windows

Upstream reworked device-lost handling (resources are Options, errors are
propagated, a failed resize invalidates the devices, atlas lookups of dropped
textures return None) but still panics when recovery fails after its five
quick retries; a driver restart, sleep/wake or driver update can take longer.
Instead: the platform logs the failure and tries again on the next vsync; a
window renderer that could not recover keeps the new devices and retries on
its next draw (drawing nothing meanwhile, building the swap chain at the
window's current size); and after recovery the window's acrylic blur, which
the driver restart drops, is applied again (switched off first: the same
accent again may be ignored).

